/**
 * util.tks — the SECOND source file of the debugger proof-of-concept, added for the
 * cross-file line-table crumb. `multi.s` places `add` here (file 2 of its `.debug_line`
 * file table) while `main` stays in `hello.tks` (file 1), so a `bt` that resolves each
 * frame to its OWN `.tks` file proves the DWARF writer's multi-file support end to end.
 *
 * Like `hello.tks`, THIS FILE IS NEVER COMPILED: it is the source the hand-written DWARF in
 * `multi.s` points at, and the DWARF writer (`src/backend/dwarf.tks`) reproduces that same
 * file table byte for byte through `line_header_body`'s file list and the per-row `set_file`
 * opcode. `add` is declared on line 17 and its first body statement is line 18 — the row the
 * cross-file harness breaks on.
 *
 * @see multi.s                 the object whose two-file DWARF names this file as file 2
 * @see d1_multifile_harness.sh  the gdb harness that asserts the cross-file backtrace
 * @since 0.3.1 debugger proof-of-concept
 */
fn add(a: i32, b: i32) -> i32 {
    let s = a + b
    s
}
